From: ccgreg@showme.missouri.edu
Newsgroups: comp.admin.policy
Subject:  A new collection of Acceptable Use Policies
Date: Fri, 09 Dec 94 11:53:36 CST
Message-ID: <17087A74BS86.CCGREG@mizzou1.missouri.edu>

    http://musie.phlab.missouri.edu/Policy/index.html
 
links my collection of over 100 university computing and network acceptable
use policies.  This includes fresh copies of many items found at EFF,
Rice, and New Mexico. I've found > 20 policies created or significantly
revised in 1994.  The collection includes links to other collections
and resources.
 
As you'd guess, I am helping revise my own institution's policies to account
for changes in technology and law, to deal with the many LANs and information
services connected to our backbone, to address liability, and to inform users
of rights, responsibilities risks, and recourses.
 
I am continuing to add links and copies of policies to this collection.
I expect soon to be placing drafts and archived discussions of our own new
policy out there.  Although many of the documents were in nice html form, I
reduced them to least common denominator, ~80-column text & DOS-style names.
 
If you notice omissions, mistakes, or obsolete items in this collection, I'd
appreciate notification!
 
As several other such collectors can affirm, it's hard to keep up to date on
these, even with URLs!  Hence, I don't intend to maintain this collection
beyond its usefulness to my institution.  I hope though, that it will benefit
service providers and users at least for a few months.
 
-Greg  Johnson <ccgreg@showme.missouri.edu>
 Campus Computing, University of Missouri-Columbia

